      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "sm-hero",
          "type": "hero",
          "title": "Sunset Moonland",
          "subtitle": "A place that can become home before you realize you stopped leaving."
        },
        {
          "id": "sm-prose",
          "type": "prose",
          "heading": "The place",
          "paragraphs": [
            "Sunset Moonland is not important because it has escaped hardship. Its importance comes from a social fabric where the personal still reaches the system.",
            "Its history accumulates across eras: exile, rediscovery, settlement, and finally the arrival of people who were only trying to pass through."
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "sm-timeline",
          "type": "timeline",
          "heading": "Layers of the place",
          "items": [
            {
              "id": "sm-t1",
              "label": "≈ 500 years earlier",
              "title": "An exile finds the land",
              "summary": "A Luminary child in permanent exile withdraws here and slowly changes."
            },
            {
              "id": "sm-t2",
              "label": "Before the Cessation",
              "title": "A fisherman returns",
              "summary": "A storm reveals the place; he later comes back with his wife."
            },
            {
              "id": "sm-t3",
              "label": "After the Cessation",
              "title": "A community forms",
              "summary": "Travelers begin to stay."
            }
          ]
        },
