          "id": "canvas-hero",
          "type": "hero",
          "title": "The Obscured Canvas",
          "subtitle": "The map can be correct without being complete."
        },
        {
          "id": "canvas-prose",
          "type": "prose",
          "paragraphs": [
            "The canvas is not an argument against knowledge. The marks are useful, often beautiful, and frequently correct.",
            "The error begins when their density makes the unmarked space impossible to perceive."
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "canvas-quote",
          "type": "quote",
          "text": "The paper was always white. We just couldn't see it anymore."
